62
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,000
The settings in this window are divided into two pieces.

63
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,000
In the options above, you can see the settings for the drag range.

64
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Here you can set the soft selection of the reduction type, the range and the degree of reduction.

65
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
The display range brush is randomly opened.

66
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:11,000
When you move the mouse, you will see two circles that indicate the soft selection.

67
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:17,000
The outer circle indicates the range of soft selection, and the position of the inner circle indicates the degree of reduction.

68
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
Now we turn on the full weight display.

69
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:23,000
When the full weight display is turned on, the part of the soft selection will show green.

70
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,000
The reduction type is divided into two types, the curve and the straight line.

71
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,000
The curve and curve are different in different reduction types.

72
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
In addition, the curve is also affected by the degree of reduction.

73
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:40,000
Now let's set the soft selection range and the degree of reduction to the highest to see the difference between the two reduction types.

74
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,000
When we set it to the straight line, the center range of soft selection is very small.

75
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:48,000
When we set it to the curve, the center range of soft selection is wider.

76
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
When we set it to the curve, the center range of soft selection is larger.

77
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
We return all the values to default settings.

78
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:00,000
There are two methods of measuring the range, surface measurement or straight measurement.

79
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
When the measurement method is set to the surface, the soft selection will be applied to the surface of the plate you click with the soft selection brush.

80
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Therefore, your choice will only work on the selected plate.

81
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
If the measurement range is set to the line,

82
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:19,000
the soft selection will be applied to all the 3D spaces.

83
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:24,000
This measurement method is more suitable for soft selection of multi-layered clothing.

84
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:33,000
By clicking on the button that only works for selected panels, your soft selection will only work for selected panels.

85
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,000
It is not affected by the range measurement method of selection.

86
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:41,000
This option is very effective for panels that are glued together after some simulation.

